HST Office: the office no longer crashes on quit when a mail merge engine is still held over UNO (Writer).

com.sun.star.text.MailMerge loads its DocumentURL as a hidden document and closes it in its destructor. A client
that still holds the engine when the office quits (Trộn thư's "Trộn ra văn bản" over UNO, released when the URP
bridge goes away at shutdown) had that destructor run after Writer's module was gone: the default frame format's
attributes found no pool default, SIGSEGV in SwDoc::~SwDoc (lcl_DelFormatIndices), seen on Linux with 1.0.2 and
26.8.3.1. The engine now also closes its document when the office terminates (a terminate listener on the Desktop,
in the new hst::sw::MailMergeTerminationGuard); the destructor disarms it and closes as before.

License: the new files sw/source/uibase/inc/hstmailmergetermination.hxx and
sw/source/uibase/uno/hstmailmergetermination.cxx are LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary; the upstream files remain under
their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-mail-merge-engine-at-quit.py.
